    feat(agents): add `entire agent-help`, point agents at it instead of a stale string

    Coding agents didn't know the currently-installed entire command surface, so they
    guessed flags or asked for the repo name while already inside the repo (after
    --repo/--branch were added to `entire trail`). Rather than shipping more skills
    (which churn user repos, cost context, and raise wrong-pick risk), make the live
    CLI document itself.

    - New `entire agent-help [command...]`: agent-facing usage rendered live from the
      Cobra tree, so it always matches the installed binary. Bare prints a "when to
      use entire / which subcommand" map + the auto-detected repo + the no-ask rule;
      `agent-help <command>` prints that command's exact current flags/subcommands;
      --json. Visible so agents without a context-injection channel can find it via
      `entire help`. Hidden commands opt in via Annotations[agentHelpAnnotation]
      (trail); deprecated/help excluded.

    - Repoint the existing first-turn context injection from a hardcoded trail string
      to a pointer at `entire agent-help` that names the auto-detected repo (read from
      the already-loaded session scope; no network/API at turn start) and carries
